config INFINEON_SMIF_OCTAL
	bool "Use Infineon SEMPER Octal NOR flash (PSE84 only)"
	depends on SOC_SERIES_PSE84
	help
	  Route SMIF0 on KIT_PSE84_EVAL through the 128 MB Infineon SEMPER
	  S28HS01GTGZBHI030 Octal NOR flash on chip-select 0 in OPI DDR mode
	  instead of the default 16 MB S25FS128S Quad NOR on chip-select 1.
	  This selects the alternate cycfg_qspi_memslot_octal.c file (emitted
	  by the ModusToolbox QSPI Configurator with the pre-canned
	  "Octal DDR Hybrid at Bottom 25 MHz" preset) and changes the flash
	  base address layout to match the octal 64 MB per-aperture SMIF0 map.

	  The Octal and Quad flashes on this board share DQ0..3 so only one
	  can be electrically active at a time — selecting this symbol
	  commits the whole boot chain (storage, m33s_xip, m33_xip, m55_xip)
	  to the octal chip.

	  EXPERIMENTAL — boot-from-octal requires the M33 secure image to
	  reconfigure SMIF from the ROM-default mode to OPI DDR during its
	  own early init, from SRAM-resident code. See the octal enablement
	  plan at zephyr_workspace/PSE84_OCTAL_FLASH_ENABLEMENT_PLAN.md.

